  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scoping Study on Waste Management and Circular Economy Sector Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to develop a scoping study to obtain a comprehensive overview of Indonesia&#x2019;s circular economy sector, by taking stocks of lessons learned from previous Dutch waste projects and existing local and international initiatives in the country. This will include an assessment of the needs of Indonesian public and private stakeholders and where Dutch actors could have a stronger focus. The study will identify if there are opportunities for government-to-government (G2G), business-to-government (B2G), business-to-business (B2B) and knowledge-to-knowledge (K2K) cooperation between the Netherlands and Indonesia in the area of circular economy.</narrative>
  </description>
